the Department of Recreation and Events to rehabilitate and repurpose the pump house seizing upon this opportunity will solve many problems number one it will save the pump house from further talks of demolition to lose this vital link to our pioneer heritage would be a profound cultural loss to our community the many winters of abandonment has left this structure vulnerable and the urgency to find a solution for its reuse is acute number two Mr sanchez and his clean and safe team will finally have a consolidated space to store their equipment as well as have a place to use the restroom eat their lunch and conduct a meeting this crew works very hard to keep our downtown looking beautiful and

they deserve a dignified space in which to conduct their business number three the greenway restoring integrity to the pump house will have the adjacent benefit of opening up a proper path that would finally connect bikers and walkers safely to downtown currently the greenway path dead ends at Ames Avenue forcing bikers and walkers to navigate Lincolnway in order to reach downtown number four the wetlands this land was developed back in 2012 for the Capitol Basin Drainage Project as a means of naturally cleaning storm water and it's currently fenced off um this land has the potential to be another great outdoor space for public enjoyment within this city train enthusiasts could have a park-like environment from which to view the trains because as of right

now they are relegated to the parking lot at Benton 15th Street in addition this wetlands area also just so happens to be the land upon which the original tent city of Cheyenne was born proper care and maintenance of this land would be a memorial to the courage the vision and the character of those who founded this great city i cannot think of a better department to have boots on the ground on this land than the recreation and events department led by Mr sanchez in conclusion rehabilitating the pump house will not only provide the clean and safe team with a home base it will help connect the greenway help restore the wetlands and potentially create a new park space and

